From e6376c838d651e3611d7edc896de89ff213227c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:50:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): the profile owner runs the dispatcher's model
 tier pin [daveey]

Upstream moved card execution to the profile owner (workers are -m hermes_cli.kanban_worker_client
and the owner re-reads the card), so the fork's tier pin, set on the in-memory claimed task and
recorded as the run's model_tier event, no longer reached the turn; nor did the class-selector
rule (provider auto). owner_model_pin() reads this run's model_tier event (else the row's
overrides) and applies worker_model_args' class rule; build_kanban_policy uses it.
---
 gateway/session_kanban.py                    |  5 +++-
 hermes_cli/kanban_model_tier.py              | 25 ++++++++++++++++++++
 tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_model_tier.py   | 24 +++++++++++++------
 tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_pin_provider.py | 18 ++++----------
 tests/plugins/test_kanban_model_override.py  |  9 +++++++
 5 files changed, 60 insertions(+), 21 deletions(-)

